WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.670
Clyde, thank you for being here.

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.140
Tell us what have we got here?

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.421
Well, we have a Chinchilla from Peru.

00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:08.870
I thought that was an
affluent rat, you had there.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:09.703
(audience laughs)

00:00:09.703 --> 00:00:11.487
A rat that had come into some money.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:14.050
I've heard of... this is a Chinchilla.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.740
I know the Chinchilla coats.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.090
This was the animal they used
to make Chinchilla coats.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.430
And you can tell this...

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.840
So he'd go like over here

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.160
in this part of the coat right here.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.960
No, I'm kidding, I like animals too.

00:00:28.058 --> 00:00:32.450
This is incredible, they feel so soft.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.977
Very, very dense follicles of hair.

00:00:34.977 --> 00:00:37.110
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.970
This is not so soothing
for the Chinchilla,

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.950
but for me, very calming.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.390
This is what I do before every show,

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.830
as I have a Chinchilla
brought to me and I...

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.663
(Conan sighs)

00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:46.927
... soothing.

00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:48.020
Very nice.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.090
This animal very seldom even drinks,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.310
and it, it would never
take a bath in water,

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.520
because high up in the Andes it's cold.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.400
Right.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.448
The follicles are so dense,

00:00:57.448 --> 00:00:59.980
it would probably never dry
out and would actually die,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.110
so it bathes in dust.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.070
Bathes in dust?

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.990
And if you put this animal in our...

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.005
I thought that was a shake and bake,

00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.400
(audience laughs)

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.880
cook it up, is this extra
crispy or Cajun spice?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.430
So if I put the Chinchilla in here,

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.340
it will take a dust bath?

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.400
I think he will, yes.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.893
Alright, this is a amazing.

00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:23.182
(audience coos)

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.689
Oh, that's great television right there.

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:28.740
(Audience laughs)

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.103
And he's done, that was it?

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.010
That's it?

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.192
You can't just take a...

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.700
and then it leaves the pan
and... that's nice Clyde,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.915
throw it back into the dust.

00:01:36.915 --> 00:01:37.748
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.748 --> 00:01:38.860
This is the only way they can stay clean,

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.880
is to basically roll in dust,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.030
and many other animals do this as well.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.630
Is it soothing for the animal?

00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.993
This is the Chinchilla at a four star spa.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.616
A little massage right there.

00:01:50.616 --> 00:01:53.190
(Conan sings)

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.019
You must calm Chinchilla
calm, that's incredible.

00:01:56.019 --> 00:01:58.690
Let me show you something
else I brought along.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:01:59.950
Let me show you something else,

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.140
alright, that sounded sinister,

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.440
when you said it that way.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.470
I guess he's just chilling
out right here, look at this.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.373
Just hanging out, he
can hang out, he's okay.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.387
I hope that guy works for you.

00:02:11.387 --> 00:02:12.748
(audience laughs)

00:02:12.748 --> 00:02:15.168
That was an audience
member that just came down.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.480
'I want a Chinchilla.'

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.313
Oh my God, look at this.

00:02:17.313 --> 00:02:21.460
I took a group of people to
Tanzania on a Safari in June,

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.200
and these are found in Tanzania,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.186
in the Rocky areas of rather dry,

00:02:26.186 --> 00:02:28.250
almost desert like conditions.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.083
Yes.

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.280
And it's called a Tailless whip scorpion

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.540
or some people call them
Cave dwelling spiders.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.580
But, wait, wait, wait, which is it,

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.940
a spider or a scorpion?

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:38.903
Damned if I know.

00:02:38.903 --> 00:02:39.736
(audience laughs)

00:02:39.736 --> 00:02:40.610
I honestly...

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.780
Wait, you're whipping out a bug

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.860
and it may be a scorpion,
but you're not sure?

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.170
I don't think it's a scorpion.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:49.062
Well, thanks for the scientific breakdown.

00:02:49.062 --> 00:02:50.730
(sarcastically) I don't
know, it might be a scorpion.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.563
I'm not sure.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.500
How about if I put it on you?

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.710
Alright, okay I'm scared of these things.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.740
They are poisonous.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.470
(everyone screams)

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.612
It's on my crotch.

00:03:01.612 --> 00:03:02.445
(audience laughs)

00:03:02.445 --> 00:03:04.970
Off crotch, off crotch.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.440
Okay, look at that.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.740
Wait, that's great, yeah, that's nice.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.734
Why do you put them on people?

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.850
(Conan screams)

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.460
Okay, look, it's clinging to you.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.690
Alright, do you wanna put it on my hair?

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:19.180
Put it on my hair, all bugs
like my hair, I've found.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.620
It's not sticking is it?

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.467
Oh my God, oh my god, it just...

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.210
What's it doing, why is it...

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.550
Why is it on my... it's
on my wrist right now.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.730
It may be extending it's fangs.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.010
I'm being very still,
it's doing something.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.320
It's like probing my wrist right now.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.659
It's taking my pulse.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:36.816
(audience exclaims)

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.686
They actually do have venom.

00:03:38.686 --> 00:03:41.018
(audience laughs)

00:03:41.018 --> 00:03:43.550
Are you an idiot, what
do you mean it has venom?

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.600
Isn't the wrist the shallowest
portion of the body?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.640
So if a spider, a venomous spider,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.360
or scorpion was to attack me,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.030
the wrist might be the most lethal place.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:53.900
It will be the main line.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.426
Yeah, incredible, what a
wonderful demonstration.

00:03:56.426 --> 00:03:57.840
(audience laughs)

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.720
Should we remove the spiders please?

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:00.682
That's great.

00:04:00.682 --> 00:04:02.770
Or scorpions or whatever they are.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.410
How are we going to get
this one off without it...

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.910
bite or it's okay?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:06.743
It's going into the... okay,

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:08.720
it almost went into the sleeve,

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.946
which it thought of as
a pale, freckled cave.

00:04:10.946 --> 00:04:11.860
(audience laughs)

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.693
Alright, what's next?

00:04:12.693 --> 00:04:13.526
Let's keep this moving Clyde.

00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:16.490
Okay, here's another
potentially dangerous animal.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.366
I thought you meant her.

00:04:17.366 --> 00:04:20.199
(audience laughs)

00:04:25.286 --> 00:04:26.177
(Conan exclaims)

00:04:26.177 --> 00:04:27.240
What is this, I was clowning around

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.800
and I didn't see you bring out this thing.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:29.633
What is it?

00:04:29.633 --> 00:04:30.466
Accurately enough,

00:04:30.466 --> 00:04:32.250
it's called a black headed
Python from Australia.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.680
And these animals don't get quite as large

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.330
as some of the Asian and African Pythons.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.130
They get about eight feet long
and they're constrictors...

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.575
Oh, constrictors, good.

00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:43.720
(audience laughs)

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.354
Put around neck and then
mention the constricting part.

00:04:46.354 --> 00:04:47.557
(audience laughs)

00:04:47.557 --> 00:04:50.330
When they are ready to kill
prey, they wrap around it,

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.750
they squeeze it tightly,

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:55.926
and the animal dies of
suffocation or cardiac arrest.

00:04:55.926 --> 00:04:57.269
That's great.

00:04:57.269 --> 00:04:58.730
(audience laughs)

00:04:58.730 --> 00:04:59.563
That's really great.

00:04:59.563 --> 00:05:01.770
It is constricting a little bit
right now around the throat.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.710
Is that because it senses that I'm scared

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.543
and it's squeezing.

00:05:04.543 --> 00:05:05.810
I think he's afraid of falling,

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.070
he wants to wrap around very tightly.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.830
Okay, alright, so I should support him,

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.790
now, could it bite you in the face,

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.400
if I jammed this into your head right now?

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.560
(audience laughs)

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.433
If I came at you with this
would it bite you in the head?

00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:17.351
It could, yes he could.

00:05:17.351 --> 00:05:18.480
So there's a chance

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.022
he would bite you in the head
while it was strangling me.

00:05:20.022 --> 00:05:20.855
(audience laughs)

00:05:20.855 --> 00:05:23.500
But, it probably would
turn around and bite you

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.241
because you have the
tail end, and you know...

00:05:26.241 --> 00:05:27.430
But at the last second,

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.480
the Chinchilla springs from its dust bath

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.406
and saves me, alright.

00:05:32.406 --> 00:05:35.030
He could consume the Chinchilla.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.520
They swallow their prey whole.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.929
Their jaws distend enough

00:05:37.929 --> 00:05:39.980
that this animal could swallow
something as long as...

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.303
Do you ever make these
animals fight each other?

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.440
Is that as HBO kind of thing, Cinemax?

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.440
No we don't.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.630
Fox TV, definitely, alright.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.540
Do you want to, maybe
we should remove this.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.050
Maybe we could hang him
on the Christmas tree

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:52.952
as an ornament.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.120
(audience laughs)

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:54.953
Hi, how are you?

00:05:54.953 --> 00:05:56.340
This animal was confiscated

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.240
by the U.S. fish and wildlife service.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.140
It was an illegal animal
brought into this country.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.283
That animal is a criminal, you're saying?

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.450
The person who brought it in.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.844
Oh, someone brought it in
illegally, it was confiscated,

00:06:08.844 --> 00:06:10.610
and then you went to the Lost and Found.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.738
It went to the Lowry Park
Zoo where it lives today.

00:06:13.738 --> 00:06:15.120
I think we have time for one more,

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.250
and this is... oh wow, look at this.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.774
I got this one, this
looks to me like an Owl.

00:06:19.774 --> 00:06:20.750
I need a glove, I think.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.650
That's an owl, there's a glove here.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.180
I get a glove, alright.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.130
Now tell me about this Owl.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:26.963
This looks like an Owl to me.

00:06:26.963 --> 00:06:29.725
Yeah, this is a Eurasian Eagle Owl.

00:06:29.725 --> 00:06:32.444
Owls are broken into two groups.

00:06:32.444 --> 00:06:35.020
The typical Owls and the Eagle owls,

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.350
our Great Horned Owl, in fact,

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.050
is very closely related to this animal.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.740
And they really can
turn their heads around

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.077
like 360 degrees, right?

00:06:41.077 --> 00:06:42.970
Well, not 360 but about 270.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.303
I'm pretty sure it's 360.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.612
(audience laughs)

00:06:45.612 --> 00:06:47.896
Let's compromise, about 310 degrees.

00:06:47.896 --> 00:06:50.088
Is it true that their heads detach...

00:06:50.088 --> 00:06:51.057
(audience laughs)

00:06:51.057 --> 00:06:52.610
... and there's candies inside?

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.820
I've just been told...

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.450
I don't know as much about animals as you,

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.040
but this is a... look at the eyes.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.051
Tell us about the eyes Clyde.

00:06:59.051 --> 00:06:59.908
(Conan 'hoos')

00:06:59.908 --> 00:07:02.740
Well, first of all, they can't
move their eyes very much.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.300
It's ignoring me.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.810
They're positioned with boney rings

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.350
that give them far vision.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:09.183
Yes.

00:07:09.183 --> 00:07:11.240
And it's almost binocular.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.480
It's excellent for, if
you're a predator like this,

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.020
and you're looking for prey
animals at some distance.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:22.020
In fact if you'd like to see
an example of how well they see

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.860
we could put that glove on your hand.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.620
I got the glove on, yeah.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:26.600
I thought this was for a medical exam.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.060
Do we have a piece of meat back here?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.550
We have meat, do we have some meat here

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.230
or just a little piece of meat?

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.710
What is this we're using?

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.520
Make a little clucking noise if you would,

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.470
just to get his attention.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.660
You just want me to look stupid.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.330
That has nothing to do with this.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.580
Do a clucking noise?

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:40.910
Okay, and it's going to...

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.000
Okay, this is cool.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.582
Alright, let's see what happens.

00:07:43.582 --> 00:07:44.692
(Conan clucks)

00:07:44.692 --> 00:07:46.023
These are silent flyers.

00:07:46.023 --> 00:07:48.940
(Everyone screams)

00:07:52.255 --> 00:07:55.088
(Audience cheers)

00:08:07.185 --> 00:08:10.705
Wow, what an unprofessional show.

00:08:10.705 --> 00:08:12.632
(Audience laughs)

00:08:12.632 --> 00:08:13.800
Look at that.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.050
I love that camera work there.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:16.920
Well, should we leave it there?

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.892
I think they've retrieved it,

00:08:18.892 --> 00:08:21.642
and it's got a woman's wig with it.

00:08:21.642 --> 00:08:24.475
(Audience cheers)

00:08:39.982 --> 00:08:42.565
(Conan clucks)

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.140
This thing is blind.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:50.117
It's got the biggest eyes
in the world, and it's like,

00:08:50.117 --> 00:08:52.717
"I'm sorry, I'm not getting
it, they're not seeing."

